From 4653658cb54fb8bc81d2b068e5823d870c6cf683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:14:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/28] WIP qwen4exp: sparse MTP-draft attention (QSA), default
 ON

The qwen4exp MTP draft attended dense over the whole cache; the trunk attends
sparse QSA.  At depth the single dense draft layer costs more than all twelve
sparse trunk layers, so route the draft through the same QSA machinery.

Three coupled changes (the reference design):
  - load_arch_hparams inherits the trunk compress ratio for the nextn layer
    (the converted GGUF leaves it 0; the sidecar ships blk.N.indexer.*)
  - create_memory gives the qwen4exp MTP context a hybrid-idx memory (attn +
    idx caches, no recurrent layers) instead of a plain KV cache
  - graph_mtp takes its attention input from build_inp_mem_hybrid and builds
    top_k via build_qsa_top_k, attending through build_attn_qsa

An empty recurrent child cannot service a partial seq_rm (its rollback path
needs a snapshot that was never written) and spams the non-consecutive-position
warning on speculative positions, so llama_memory_hybrid_idx and
llama_memory_recurrent::find_slot learn to skip / stay quiet when no layer
bound a state tensor.

Measured on gfx1151 (qwen4exp IQ4_NL f16 KV, MTP n3, -b/-ub 2048):
  prefill  pp150K 927.0 -> 990.8 t/s (+6.9 %) with a 32K depth gate
  decode   a loss at every measured depth (16K -13 %, 40K -15 %, 150K -16 %)

The arm is therefore opt-in (LLAMA_MTP_SPARSE=1): the prefill gate is depth
based (LLAMA_MTP_SPARSE_MIN_KV, default 32768) and the decode arm is off
(LLAMA_MTP_SPARSE_DECODE=1 opts in).  Default off because at 40K the sparse
prefill changes the greedy text while the dense draft matches plain (the
draft's different proposals expose a target verify/rollback near-tie), so the
"plain == draft-mtp" contract is not met where the prefill arm pays; at 5K all
three arms are byte-identical (3553e76d3a9e) and the MTP acceptance is
unchanged (0.85035).

Op oracles unchanged: FLASH_ATTN_QSA 26/26, GATED_DELTA_NET 46/46; width probe
PASS on qwen4exp f16.
